{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Feature Vector.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Feature Vector.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"feature vector feature vector","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Feature Vector.md","fileName":"Feature Vector.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Feature Vector","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 16:28\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Speech and Acoustic Modeling]] · [[Feature Engineering Foundations]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Speech and Acoustic Modeling","Feature Engineering Foundations","Speech Frame","Acoustic Model","aiassistants.epub","featureengineeringformachinelearninganddataanalytics.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Feature Vector.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Feature Vector.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"feature vector feature vector","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Feature Vector.md","fileName":"Feature Vector.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Feature Vector","heading":"Feature Vector","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A feature vector is an ordered set of numerical measurements representing one observation. In speech recognition, it commonly summarizes the spectral properties of a short [[Speech Frame]].\n\nA sequence of feature vectors is more compact and model-ready than the original waveform. The [[Acoustic Model]] uses the sequence to estimate which phonetic states most plausibly produced the signal.\n\nMore generally, a feature vector assigns one value to each feature selected for a data object. Using a fixed feature set places heterogeneous objects into a common coordinate representation, allowing learning algorithms to compare, partition, or predict them.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Speech and Acoustic Modeling","Feature Engineering Foundations","Speech Frame","Acoustic M